```css
.form-field.correct .feedback-msg {
  display: block;
  color: var(--correct);
}

.form-field.incorrect .feedback-msg {
  display: block;
  color: var(--incorrect);
}
```

So when the form-field has `.correct`, ALL `.feedback-msg` elements inside are shown. 

I see the issue now—I need to consolidate to a single `.feedback-msg` per question and use JavaScript to update the text content dynamically, letting the parent class handle the color styling. I'll update the HTML structure and JavaScript to use a single feedback message element per question, setting its content dynamically based on whether the answer is correct or incorrect.

